WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
1623.

2
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.270
Shakespeare's plays are printed together,

3
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.800
in the First Folio.

4
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.580
Here's a famous line from Hamlet,
spelled exactly as the Folio prints it.

5
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.140
A modern edition prints: "The heart-ache,

6
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.910
and the thousand natural
shocks That flesh is heir to".

7
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.070
Same language.

8
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.330
Same words, same meanings.

9
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.590
So why does the Folio's
spelling look so wild?

10
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.010
In this mission, you'll place
Shakespeare in the periods of English,

11
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.040
from Old English to now.

12
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.220
You'll see how the
printing press, from 1476,

13
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.910
spread written English.

14
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.780
And you'll hear how
pronunciation moved, too.

15
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.080
Your mission: work out why the
Folio's spelling is so wild.
